  "title": "Chapter 4 – Microbiology",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "ghnpq4d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Microorganisms are broadly classified into Bacteria, Viruses, Fungi, and Parasites.",
        "Sterilization and Disinfection are fundamental techniques required to eliminate or reduce pathogens.",
        "Immunity serves as the primary defense mechanism against infectious microbial agents.",
        "Hospital Acquired Infections (Nosocomial Infections) represent critical safety concerns in healthcare environments."
      ],
      "id": "4489ou8"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Microbe Categories",
          "value": "4 Core Types",
          "icon": "book"
