          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "jqg9c8u"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "94d09q9",
      "content": "Microbiology is the study of microorganisms such as bacteria, viruses, fungi, and parasites. In nursing examinations like RRB Nursing, questions frequently come from microbial classification, modes of transmission, sterilization methods, immunity, and hospital-acquired infections."
    },
    {
